{"title":"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f019000e7e4e14a3379d05327eb7db704d2897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> price reduction, what increase does it take to restore the original price?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b3913d5fd3abbcbc40bdcd74cd4b700fa906e2c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }p\\%  \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }\\frac p{1-p}\\% \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } (100-p)\\% \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{100p}{100+p}\\% \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{100p}{100-p}\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"624\" height=\"41\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the unknown be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  Initially, we have something of price <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />.  We reduce the price by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f019000e7e4e14a3379d05327eb7db704d2897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4797f54c3da9ad6564c698fc2b765fdc384478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q - Q\\cdot p\\% = Q - Q\\frac p{100} = Q\\cdot\\frac{100 - p}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"307\" height=\"38\" />.  We now increase this price by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de1a36d69a7028480a87b712a7141c651398a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e1488d351dfebb04a44a508341d04ccbbb7407eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(Q\\cdot\\frac{100 - p}{100}\\right) + \\left(Q\\cdot\\frac{100 - p}{100}\\right)\\cdot x\\% = \\left(Q\\cdot\\frac{100 - p}{100}\\right)\\cdot(1 + x\\%) = Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"556\" height=\"43\" />  We can cancel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> from both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/450e97851fafe692096440dc3f44201eb5c75a9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100 - p}{100}\\cdot\\left(1 + x\\%\\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"179\" height=\"38\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d94ec37ab5b247add8aea80d9cc5c66bebe2f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + x\\% = \\frac{100}{100 - p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce74132ad8169e770f2bea0eab51f251e5dc2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\% = \\frac{p}{100 - p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"111\" height=\"36\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f43492594caca6272abd16c1e89b242b885a6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{100p}{100 - p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"95\" height=\"41\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/270d869de88abb3c05be5b3740413f8f19c6aa8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E) \\ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Alternatively, select a particular value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that the five answer choices all have different values.  For instance, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b0673a4c47bae6cdf8de9342992c31f47087636c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. Thus if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> dollars was the original price, after the price reduction, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollars. We need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollars. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2e93ed2c499496ac63cdfb2bab9d267712b342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90(1+x\\%)=100 \\Longrightarrow x\\%=\\frac{10}{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"250\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa40e6383a4451d768d8a20c0ef6abe61ba06930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{100 \\cdot 10}{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" />.  This only matches up with answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/270d869de88abb3c05be5b3740413f8f19c6aa8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E) \\ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> when we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d726acbcc434a2af56b24e08f3ad06e7d1f6ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_5\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 5\">Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_7\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 7\">Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam\">Back to Exam</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018113259\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 78/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4570/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3425:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018113259 and revision id 86278. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}